.TH FEATURE:TOGGLE 1 "June 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
feature:toggle \- Manage advanced feature flags, canary rollout percentages, and evaluate Telemetry Kill Switch status.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBphp spp.php feature:toggle\fR [\fB\-\-flag=\fI<name>\fR] [\fB\-\-enable=\fI<true|false>\fR] [\fB\-\-canary=\fI<percentage>\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBfeature:toggle\fR command provides enterprise deployment decoupling. It allows systems administrators and developers to enable or disable advanced features dynamically, rollout experimental features to a percentage of active users (canary releases), and monitor the real-time status of the automated Telemetry Kill Switch.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-flag=\fI<name>\fR
Exact name of the feature flag to target.
.TP
\fB\-\-enable=\fI<true|false>\fR
Explicitly enable or disable the feature flag.
.TP
\fB\-\-canary=\fI<percentage>\fR
Set the percentage of traffic (0-100) to expose to the canary release.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
1. \fBStrict SAPI Guarding\fR: Validates that execution occurs in a secure CLI environment via \fIisCLIOnly(): bool\fR.
.PP
2. \fBDynamic Flag Mutation\fR: Updates the in-memory or persisted configuration state within \fIFeatureManager\fR.
.PP
3. \fBCanary Hashing\fR: Uses deterministic hashing (\fIcrc32\fR) of the flag name and user ID to ensure consistent canary routing.
.PP
4. \fBTelemetry Kill Switch Check\fR: Queries \fIOpenTelemetryExporter\fR for active error counts associated with the flag scope. If errors exceed the threshold, the flag is marked as \fITRIGGERED\fR and automatically disabled.
